IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 1118 of 2020
CITATION: (2020) 5 SCC 1
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Arun Mishra, Indira Banerjee, Vineet Saran, M.R. Shah, S. Ravindra Bhat

PARTIES:
Sushila Aggarwal vs State (NCT of Delhi)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 438 CrPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
anticipatory bail, time limitation, protection till trial, special circumstances

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Constitution bench held that anticipatory bail under Section 438 CrPC should not be invariably limited to a fixed time period and can continue until the conclusion of the trial.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 438 CrPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

